<description>&lt;p&gt;Egypt reopened its embassy in Tripoli, restoring diplomatic ties after a 12-year gap. ISIS militants killed a young Christian man in Libya after he refused to deny Jesus, and the WHO identified 111 children with malnutrition in Qatrun, warning of deteriorating health services. Migrant vessels departing from Libya have suffered deadly shipwrecks off Crete, with at least 20 migrants killed in recent incidents. Libya and Chad signed the final document of the CEN-SAD Executive Council meeting, and Egypt is seeking faster progress on Libya gas, refining and power projects. Combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxNN1RnOEJkbERKWVhHcXc2NkV6c3RSWS1aVHk1SFhRZExUU3VkWWo3dnVXOFFsNDZxUWRYS2tha3M5Njl0QUVKNGktR3NITURSazV6bzVBazJvWDhDbGFzNHVWRnhjWlprclhoVnJzOXFWVjRyYTY4dU40dHBaZGpEako1NmtqLXBWY3BaV0hhaw?oc=5&quot;&gt;www.christiandaily.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxQRkdEWnJyMlRPQkNYamR3SmpCSWxvSkNsNGM4anlaXzB4MTEzc0dwbldVVzZrMU5YZHhrcF9RaUFEWnl3djlqSmJ1ZUI3M3ZIOUtqTVhmTWdqNFp5enFnMXBjbFNkUkgxMDBZeHF0U2VjZWxQWGxmRnV6aWFiODZDSzNGUDZJaDlpNFN1QUpWRzFUSTE4amtZcFBKMk_SAZsBQVVfeXFMT1ZwQ3pVUm41SEprdXQ5QUt3ZDJaNEQ1aTdUbGlHZlhXbkRvRG11akdwSFhUNDR2OWozM0lfbGU2TXZSQVhPcVozUGp3WTYtUlBSV255MmpYNndSN3AzQXVvS0lnc0w3d1pSeXVkR2NfeFNzdzdqY0ZSQk5KUUJWejk0eDBZWEZJSWVoakdNNm1rLUhGNVFya3hLTG8?oc=5&quot;&gt;Modern Ghana&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitwFBVV95cUxQZkJ4MnRIOVFTNFpGTlVoWXhqRUFRbVBiNmlHN2czWE5tV19ZQW13ZUlRTDRSY2tFcG83WDVoY0lJVDZ3RkpuaHpSeVR0MndXLS1xaF8tOEROQlJYT0tKbjlZUHJiWDgyRXpRdml6